                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Not sure what you are exactly referring to.. I performed the testing for this patch similar to my other patches."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "In support of this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp",
                    "line": 721,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "What's the holdup just using the new version of this code in all cases?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp",
                    "line": 721,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Currently no single-host implements the ManagedHost interface. I could however (and would rather like to) change the interface to xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.System, which at least some single-hosts configure looking at EM upstream configs.\n\nBut even then, I expect to have name mismatches between BMCWEB_REDFISH_SYSTEM_URI_NAME and what is used for the dbus object representing the computer system on at least a few platforms. In these cases the validator will fail which should be considered a regression?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp",
                    "line": 725,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This looks like it's assuming that every path hosted on the BMC is managed by the BMC.  I guess that's true for the ManagedHost interface?  Otherwise it would just be the host interface?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp",
                    "line": 725,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, that is true for the ManagedHost interface.\n\n>  Otherwise it would just be the host interface?\n\nJust for clarification, do you mean `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Item.System`?\nI guess so, if it implies that the computer system implementing it, is also managed by the bmc. Looking at the description in PDI, that is not clear to me. (In that case I suggest to update the description)\n\nAlso could we do the same assumption for `ManagerForChassis`? Meaning, everything that implements Item.Chassis, can be considered to be managed by this BMC? Otherwise I would continue investigating towards associations"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp",
                    "line": 726,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Need to add /inventory here as well.  Also dbus paths don't end in /.  The mapper returns the right call for now, but it's still incorrect."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp",
                    "line": 726,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp",
                    "line": 844,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Not loving the link to a commit that could never go in but :shrug: \n\nTODO: Fix getMainChassis for support multiple chassis, for now disable in MULTI Computer System\n\nis better IMO\n\n\nThis could also just be a separate commit"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp",
                    "line": 844,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This needs removed.  We shouldn't be pointing to Gerrit reviews in code.  If you want to point in your commit message, fine, but as written this makes it soudn like a dependency."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp",
                    "line": 844,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "This should also be removed because It won't solve this at all. Need another implementation to handle ManagerForChassis. \n\nCurrently looking into a solution via associations, but have to figure out some more details.\n\nRemoved it. Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/managers.hpp",
                    "line": 860,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I'd like to see this large lambda (with no captures, so could've been a normal method call) cleaned up before we continue increasing its scope.  If you want to do it all in this one patch, that's fine, but this patch is making this already mediocre code worse."
                }
